<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-10314] Spark dataframe will get wrong schema if user executes add/drop column DDL</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-10314</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When user&#160;performs add/remove column in DDL,&#160;&#160;Spark will get the old/wrong&#160;schema.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Analyse&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Currently Spark data frame API relies on QueryEntity to construct schema, but QueryEntity in QuerySchema is a local copy of the original&#160;QueryEntity, so the original&#160;QueryEntity&#160;is not updated when modification happens.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Solution&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use GridQueryTypeDescriptor to replace QueryEntity&lt;/p&gt;</description>
